    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "d46debc7f03da7f7e60a73cf4155b0da587e174ecde14bd852183035b766e00f",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast. A private 4-hour tour of Lima, the City of Kings, begins at the Love Park in Miraflores, with its panoramic view of the Pacific, Víctor Delfín’s sculpture “The Kiss” and Gaudí-style walls inscribed with lines from Peruvian love poems. Drive past the Huaca Pucllana pyramid, a ceremonial centre of the Lima culture, and through San Isidro, the financial heart of the city, with the pre-Inca shrine of Huaca Huallamarca. Stop at the Main Square, with the Government Palace, the Municipality, the Archbishop’s Palace and the Cathedral, where Francisco Pizarro is buried; walk to the Monastery of Santo Domingo, where the remains of Saint Martin de Porres and Saint Rose of Lima rest; and end at the Larco Museum, an 18th-century mansion built over a 7th-century pre-Columbian pyramid. Free afternoon.",
      "provenance": {
